> Do they? Equally well? I always thought to effectively train your pet to
> steal, you'd have to give the reward to it, the very turn it drops
> something (which of course isn't the case, when you drop it and wait for
> the pet to eat it).

The effect on apport is greater the sooner a pet receives a reward
after dropping an item; the formula is:

  apport gain = (200 / (distance + delay))

where "distance" is the number of squares away from you it was when it
dropped the item, and "delay" is the number of turns after dropping it.

